# Topic permissions for the Phase 3 LAN broker (docs 04 and 05). Usernames and topics only: no secret is in this file, and the passwords are
# in a file outside the repository. A user that is not listed here can neither read nor write anything.
#
# The probe publishes its telemetry and listens for control messages; the bridge only reads telemetry; only the operator writes the
# control topic; the web intake process (Phase 5) may write ONE topic, force/telemetry/web-intake, which the bridge's
# force/telemetry/# subscription already covers, and reads nothing.
#
# Note that under MQTT 3.1.1 Mosquitto acknowledges a QoS 1 publish that the ACL then drops, so a denial is visible only as a message
# that never arrives (edge/mqtt_check.py tests it that way). Under MQTT 5 the PUBACK carries the reason code "Not authorized", which
# is why the intake client speaks MQTT 5 (intake/e2e_report.py shows both against Mosquitto 2.1.2).

user probe-01
topic write force/telemetry/probe-01
topic read force/control/probe-01

user force-bridge
topic read force/telemetry/#

user web-intake
topic write force/telemetry/web-intake

user operator
topic write force/control/probe-01
topic read force/#
